md:
The specification gives mitosis three jobs, and the paper asks for them by name:
• **growth**: you began as one cell;
• **replacing worn-out cells**: skin and the lining of the gut are renewed all the time;
• **repairing damaged tissue**: a cut closes because cells divide.

• give the numbers for each division: mitosis 1 division, 2 identical diploid cells; meiosis 2 divisions, 4 different haploid gametes;
• name the three uses of mitosis, and the testes and ovaries for meiosis;
• explain why gametes are haploid, following a chromosome number through meiosis, fertilisation and mitosis;
• draw or choose the cells each division makes, and every nucleus meiosis could make;
• name independent assortment, and say that it produces variation.
